# Centralized UI services

Cross-phase overlays (`InputHintPresenter`, `PartyFormationFloater`, `ItemListInventory`, `SkillUsePickerPresenter`, …) use **one scene `GameObject` + `UIDocument`** under `GameState`. Phase views **orchestrate** via static facades; they do **not** own duplicate picker trees.

**Authority:** [centralized-ui-services.md](../../docs/04-dev/centralized-ui-services.md). **Gotchas:** [centralized-ui-gotchas.md](../../docs/04-dev/centralized-ui-gotchas.md) (pop-in exit races, `IsSettling`, context-switch `HideImmediate`, detached-host tests). **Animation:** [ADR 039](../../decisions/039-uitk-dotween-show-hide.md) — DOTween via `UiToolkitTweens` + `UiTransitionSession`; BEM steady state, not USS `transition-duration`.

## `ICentralizedUiSurface` — required

Every centralized service (`GameState` child with its own `UIDocument` — see doc § Scene graph) **must** implement `ICentralizedUiSurface` on the presenter (directly or via `CentralizedUiPresentation` + internal `IPresentationDriver`).

- Facades expose `RequestedVisible`, `IsShown`, `IsSettling` — not misleading `IsOpen` / context-as-visible.
- `HideImmediate()` on phase exit, context swap, competing overlay.
- **Exception:** `ScreenFadePresenter` (imperative beat fade on `GameState.ScreenFade`).

Epic: [game#206](https://github.com/miramocha/griddungeon-game/issues/206). New services: reject PRs without the interface.

## Standalone document — required for migrations

When moving UI into this pattern, the **shipped** integration must **not**:

- `CloneTree` the service UXML into `HubHud`, `CombatHud`, `PartyMenu`, or other phase roots
- Reparent service `VisualElement` nodes into another document’s host (embedded party-menu pane hosts, `InventoryPaneHost`, …)
- Use **`worldBound` / `GeometryChangedEvent`** to position a service panel inside another `UIDocument` (“geometry dock”)

**Do instead:**

- One presenter + facade on a dedicated `GameObject` (`DevSceneComposition.Wire…`)
- Full-screen transparent modal (or other self-contained overlay chrome) at the service `sortingOrder`
- Fixed rail inset via **USS** (e.g. `tabbed-picker--rail-offset`, `left: 240px`) — not parenting into the phase shell

## Review checklist

Reject migration PRs that still have:

| Smell | Example |
|-------|---------|
| Embedded picker clone | `CloneTree(ItemListPicker.uxml)` on `HubHudView` / `CombatHudView` |
| Embedded party bag | Cloning bag picker into `PartyMenu` dialog panes instead of `ItemListInventory` |
| Cross-document dock API | `DockBag`, `UndockBag`, `SyncBagDockGeometry`, inline `style.left/top` from foreign `worldBound` |
| Local duplicate presenter | `HubShopPickerPresenter` after `ItemListInventory` ships |

**OK:** `PartyFormationFloater.ApplyFormationDockState` (exploration) / `ApplyPartyMenuFloaterDock` (party menu) — same-document context + `sortingOrder` only (not reparenting into party menu UXML).

**Shared command rail:** `CommandRail.PanelHost` is repopulated per phase. Call `CommandPanelModalSupport.ResetPanelChrome` when leaving combat or before hub/party `Populate` so `command-panel--disabled` does not leak to hub buttons.

